# Root-level safety net. Each of backend/, ml-service/, and frontend/
# already has its own .gitignore for anything specific to that service -
# this one exists as a second, broader line of defense so nothing heavy
# or secret slips in no matter where in the tree it's created from,
# using **/ so these patterns match at any depth, not just here.

# Python virtual environments and bytecode
**/.venv/
**/venv/
**/__pycache__/
**/*.pyc
**/*.pyo
**/.pytest_cache/

# Node
**/node_modules/
**/dist/
**/dist-ssr/
**/*.tsbuildinfo

# Secrets - every service's .env holds a real credential of some kind
# (DB password, JWT secret, or the Groq API key)
**/.env
!**/.env.example

# Local SQLite fallback DB files
**/*.db
**/*.sqlite3

# Logs
**/*.log
**/logs/

# Editor/OS junk
**/.vscode/
**/.idea/
**/.DS_Store
**/Thumbs.db

# The original assessment brief and planning notes - not part of the
# shipped project, kept locally for reference only
instructions/
